---
description: Use when the user says build it or fix it, or asks to build or fix something on Alis Build without naming a specific workflow.
---

Run the Alis Build "build it" / "fix it" router as described in the DBD rule's routing contract.

First infer what the user wants built or fixed from the current request, visible errors, repository context, and any available Alis Build context. If the goal is still ambiguous, ask exactly one concise clarification question: "What exactly should Alis build?"

Once the goal is clear, run `alis skills search "<clarified goal>" --json`. Present the matching skills in a concise table with columns for number, skill id, description, and when to choose it. Ask the user which skill to use, then load it with `alis skills load <id>` and follow it — the loaded skill owns execution.

If the search returns nothing, say so and offer `alis skills request` (it proposes a new skill to the Alis Build team for review) — do not fall back to listing the whole catalogue.

Do not trigger builds, defines, deploys, commits, or code edits from this router step — only the loaded skill does that, and only when its workflow requires it.
